# Admin console: True/False radios side-by-side

Boolean admin settings that use True/False `Radio` options must lay out **horizontally** (one row), not stacked vertically.

## Pattern

Wrap the pair in a flex row with horizontal gap (same idea as `admin-console-layout__radio-row`):

```scss
.radio-row {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--spacing-xl);
  // Match setting-label padding so radios top-align with the left column label
  padding-top: var(--spacing-xxs);

  // Radio defaults to width: 100%; shrink so True/False stay in one row
  > * {
    width: auto;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }
}
```

```tsx
<div className={styles['radio-row']}>
  <Radio name="setting" value="true" defaultChecked size="Medium">
    True
  </Radio>
  <Radio name="setting" value="false" size="Medium">
    False
  </Radio>
</div>
```

## Do not

- Stack True above False in a column for boolean admin settings
- Rely on `Radio`'s default `width: 100%` inside a flex row without overriding — that forces wrap onto two lines
- Strip `padding-top` from the left setting label for radio rows — keep label padding consistent and match it on the radio row instead
